  "kind": "data-integrity correction after unblinding (not an amendment of the frozen procedure)",
  "applies_to": "experiments\\phase4_frozen_protocol.json",
  "protocol_sha256": "980e2ab80e5536adff1dbe04f25bfcaadd91bce4ba647edcc7ff5bd5420bcdbd",
  "amendment_1_sha256": "c742d7eaabae9de9f0d4a3d19f50bbca62cc54e8a7d9e498ce85d714edaf2044",
  "created": "2026-11-05",
  "status": "The corrected June-October 2026 evaluation is retrospective and post-unblinding, not a new independent confirmation. The original run stays the result of the pre-registered procedure; it is not claimed to have established significance, whatever the corrected interval shows.",
  "defect": "Found after unblinding, by the post-hoc disagreement analysis (2026-11-05). The held-out assembly (heldout.assemble, version 1) added a TennisData.app row unless it linked to a TML row by matching surname-and-initial keys for both players, or by both players being in both validated crosswalks; its last guard compared resolved player ids. Players whose providers write their names differently ('Merida Aguilar D.' / 'Daniel Merida', 'Ruse G.' / 'Elena Gabriela Ruse', 'Vallejo D.' / 'Adolfo Daniel Vallejo', 'Tam Sin Hang' / 'Sin Hang Tam', ...) failed every check and were resolved to different ids, so 65 matches were added twice and updated ratings, form, inactivity and profiles twice. The TennisData.app crosswalk also linked 'Vallejo D.' (424916) to Sackmann 118808 (Daniel Vallejo, MEX, born 1984) instead of 209226 (Adolfo Daniel Vallejo, PAR, born 2004), because Sackmann files Paraguay's 2023-2026 Davis Cup matches under 118808; and TML's 'Daniel Merida' (M0N7) had no link, so his TML matches started from a new, history-less identity.",
  "fix": "heldout.assemble version 2 (version 1 kept for reproduction): a third match-linking pass on round, edition, dates and name-compatible players (never on results), with ambiguous cases left out and listed; TennisData.app <-> TML player links learned from linked matches, one-to-one, so each person has one canonical id; the unverified surname-and-initial guess removed; crosswalk conflicts listed and resolved to the TML identity; a build-stopping check for any remaining cross-source duplicate or split identity. provider_period gains a version argument; the frozen holdout and rehearse commands are pinned to version 1. No model, feature, parameter, training date, dataset, input file, or evaluation rule changed.",
  "code_base_commit": "f67c54e7cd80f87acaf773bf369ac0d8366ed495",
  "frozen_code_commit": "4f6076ef8ed3895c491e3f1d65641dc7371af964",
